      "page_title": "Recovering Work & Merge Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Server-side force-push protection is the only enforceable form of the golden rule. Conventions do not survive a bad night."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. First Five Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "rebased a shared branch",
              "coordinate, or revert instead"
            ],
            [
              "ours/theirs inverted",
              "zdiff3, read the base"
            ],
            [
              "committed conflict markers",
              "hook + git diff --check"
            ],
            [
              "--theirs on modify/delete",
              "git rm or git add explicitly"
            ],
            [
              "reset --hard mid-rebase",
              "always rebase --abort"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# .git/hooks/pre-commit",
            "git diff --cached --check || exit 1",
            "grep -rn '^<<<<<<< ' . && exit 1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Getting Work Back",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "commits lost after rebase",
              "reflog, then reset --hard"
            ],
            [
              "orphans past the reflog",
              "git fsck --lost-found"
            ],
            [
              "bad merge, unpushed",
              "reset --hard ORIG_HEAD"
            ],
            [
              "bad merge, already pushed",
              "git revert -m 1 <sha>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reflog                 # find HEAD@{n}",
            "git reset --hard HEAD@{5}  # pre-rebase tip"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Traps With Merges",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "re-merge after a revert",
              "revert the revert, then merge"
            ],
            [
              "squashed, then merged again",
              "delete and re-branch"
            ],
            [
              "dirty tree blocks rebase",
              "stash, or rebase.autoStash"
            ],
            [
              "same conflict every commit",
              "rerere before you start"
            ],
            [
              "pull invents merge commits",
              "pull.rebase or pull.ff"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Re-merging after a revert brings back nothing: the merge base already accounts for those commits, so Git sees no work to do."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Choosing Your Tool & Recovery Cheat Sheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pick Your Tool",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Reach for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "not diverged, want it in",
              "merge --ff-only"
            ],
            [
              "diverged and shared",
              "git merge"
            ],
            [
              "local, nothing pushed",
              "git rebase main"
            ],
            [
              "messy WIP before PR",
              "git rebase -i"
            ],
            [
              "feedback on an old commit",
              "--fixup + --autosquash"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Configure Once",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config --global rerere.enabled true",
            "git config --global rebase.autoStash true",
            "git config --global pull.rebase true",
            "git config merge.conflictStyle zdiff3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Reach for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "need one commit only",
              "cherry-pick -x <sha>"
            ],
            [
              "undo something public",
              "git revert, never rebase"
            ],
            [
              "built on the wrong base",
              "rebase --onto new old br"
            ],
            [
              "many replayed conflicts",
              "rerere.enabled first"
            ],
            [
              "confused which side",
              "merge.conflictStyle zdiff3"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Recovery Reflex",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git reflog` first — always, before panicking",
            "`git reset --hard <good-sha>` second",
            "Nothing committed in ~90 days is truly lost",
            "Uncommitted work is the only work you can destroy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Zero-Risk Moves",
          "items": [
            "merge: never rewrites anything",
            "revert: adds, never removes",
            "--ff-only: refuses to invent history",
            "reflog: read-only, free"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Handbook In One Line",
          "text": "Merge records what happened; rebase edits the story; fast-forward means there was no story to reconcile. Choose by who else can already see the commits."
        }
      ]
    }
