  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of GIT REBASE & MERGE. Most Git pain is one confusion: merge preserves what happened, rebase rewrites it into what you wish had happened — and the SHAs pay the price. This handbook goes down to the object level: three-way diff internals, the ort strategy, patch-ids, index stages, why ours/theirs invert during rebase, and a decision table for every integration situation. Save it for the next time a rebase halts on commit 4 of 10.",
